> flat-in-disguise types, and that a model never needs it, since it reads several factors as
> several terms. Providing a sum keeps a model of many retirements that never
> retire the landmark small, at the cost of an operation that a retirement does not need. This
> document recommends leaving it out of this entry. Should the library provide the sum of factors?

The question of [which role binds the linear part](#the-roles) is open as well.
